Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:36:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy: EarlyStrike flag, the book half (a
 military-first capital for warmongers with an early spike, as the user's
 Aztec)

The user's Aztec game (106F8550): capital built Jaguar x3, Worker,
Settler, Archer x4, Jaguar x2, kept 2 cities and no buildings, had no gold
trouble, and took Marrakesh at T54. Ours built a median of 2 military by
T50 (War, 69 games); captures went with early military.

For a candidate warmonger whose spike unit comes by turn 30 Standard
(Personality's profile, bMilitaryFirst; cached once per game in
CvPlayer::GetEarlyStrikeCoreClass), under the flag:
- capital book: the spike unit x3 (x4 if it's the warrior class, the
  starting unit counting), Worker, Settler, support x4 (archers behind a
  melee spike unit; spearmen, or warriors before Bronze Working, in front
  of a ranged one), the spike unit x2;
- research: the spike unit's tech, then the support's, then the
  warmonger list;
- small empire: no settler built or bought past the book's one (2 cities)
  until a war with a major starts, to turn 90 Standard at most;
- gold stays positive: a combat step waits while one more unit couldn't be
  kept for 10 turns (GetAffordableWarUnits(10) < 1).
War's half (the window, the declaration around T50-60, the target) reads
the same flag. Off in the bundle. Written 8:36pm ET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj2nf4FeZTEHWjvnhhA
